chapters.translation:
I say — may God guide us and you to the truth:

His saying, exalted be He: {«Praise be to God who created the heavens and the earth and made the darkness and the light; yet those who disbelieve ascribe equals to their Lord. He it is who created you from clay, then decreed a term, and a term appointed with Him; yet you doubt. And He is God in the heavens and in the earth; He knows your secret and your open deeds, and He knows what you earn.»}

And His saying: {«And to Him belongs whatever dwells in the night and the day, and He is the Hearing, the Knowing. Say: Shall I take as protector other than God, the Originator of the heavens and the earth, who feeds and is not fed? Say: I have been commanded to be the first of those who submit, and not to be of the idolaters. Say: I fear, if I disobey my Lord, the chastisement of a tremendous day. Whoever is turned away from it on that day — He has had mercy upon him; and that is the manifest triumph. And if God touches you with harm, there is no remover of it but He; and if He touches you with good, He is powerful over all things. And He is the Dominant above His servants, and He is the Wise, the Aware.»}

And His saying: {«And there is no creature on the earth, nor a bird flying with its two wings, but they are communities like yourselves. We have neglected nothing in the Book; then to their Lord they shall be gathered.»}

And His saying: {«Say: Have you considered — if God should take away your hearing and your sight and seal your hearts, what god other than God could bring them back to you? See how We turn about the signs; yet they turn away. Say: Have you considered — if the chastisement of God comes upon you suddenly or openly, will any be destroyed except the wrongdoing people?»}

And His saying: {«And with Him are the keys of the unseen; none knows them but He. And He knows what is in the land and the sea; no leaf falls but He knows it, nor any grain in the darkness of the earth, nor anything moist or dry, but it is in a clear Book. And He it is who takes you by night and knows what you have committed by day; then He raises you up therein, that a term appointed may be fulfilled. Then to Him is your return; then He will inform you of what you used to do. And He is the Dominant above His servants, and He sends guardians over you until, when death comes to one of you, Our messengers take him, and they do not fail. Then they are returned to God, their true Master. Surely His is the judgment, and He is the swiftest of reckoners. Say: Who delivers you from the darknesses of the land and the sea, when you call upon Him humbly and in secret — 'If He delivers us from this, we shall surely be of the thankful'? Say: God delivers you from it and from every distress; yet you associate partners with Him. Say: He is powerful to send upon you chastisement from above you or from beneath your feet, or to confuse you in sects and make you taste the violence of one another. See how We turn about the signs, that perhaps they may understand.»}

And His saying: {«And He it is who created the heavens and the earth in truth; and on the day He says 'Be,' it is. His word is the truth, and His is the kingdom on the day the trumpet is blown — Knower of the unseen and the witnessed; and He is the Wise, the Aware. And when Abraham said to his father Āzar: Do you take idols as gods? I see you and your people in manifest error. And thus We show Abraham the kingdom of the heavens and the earth, that he might be of those who are certain. When the night covered him, he saw a star; he said: This is my Lord. But when it set, he said: I love not those that set. When he saw the moon rising, he said: This is my Lord. But when it set, he said: If my Lord does not guide me, I shall surely be of the people who go astray. When he saw the sun rising, he said: This is my Lord; this is greater. But when it set, he said: O my people, I am innocent of what you associate. I have turned my face to Him who originated the heavens and the earth, as a ḥanīf, and I am not of the idolaters.»}

And His saying: {«Indeed, God is the Splitter of the grain and the date-stone; He brings forth the living from the dead, and the dead from the living. That is God — so how are you perverted? He is the Splitter of the dawn, and He has made the night a stillness, and the sun and the moon a reckoning. That is the decree of the Mighty, the Knowing. And He it is who made for you the stars, that you might be guided by them in the darknesses of the land and the sea. We have detailed the signs for a people who know. And He it is who originated you from a single soul — then a resting place and a depository. We have detailed the signs for a people who understand. And He it is who sends down water from the sky, and We bring forth thereby the growth of everything; and We bring forth from it green, from which We bring forth grain piled up; and from the palm-tree, from its spathe, clusters hanging low; and gardens of grapes, and olives, and pomegranates, alike and not alike. Look at their fruit when it bears fruit and ripens. Surely in that are signs for a people who believe. And they have made for God partners — the jinn — though He created them; and they have ascribed to Him sons and daughters without knowledge. Glory be to Him, and exalted be He above what they describe — Originator of the heavens and the earth. How should He have a son, when He has no consort, and He created everything, and He is Knower of all things? That is God, your Lord; there is no god but He, the Creator of everything; so worship Him, and He is Guardian over everything. Eyes do not perceive Him, but He perceives the eyes; and He is the Subtle, the Aware. There have come to you clear proofs from your Lord; so whoever sees, it is for his own soul, and whoever is blind, it is against it; and I am not a keeper over you.»}

And His saying: {«And the word of your Lord has been fulfilled in truth and justice; none can alter His words, and He is the Hearing, the Knowing.»}

And His saying: {«And your Lord is the Self-Sufficient, the Possessor of mercy. If He wills, He can remove you and cause to succeed after you whatever He wills, just as He originated you from the progeny of another people.»}

And His saying: {«And He it is who originated gardens, trellised and untrellised, and the palm-tree and the crops, diverse in their produce, and the olive and the pomegranate, alike and not alike. Eat of their fruit when they bear fruit, and give its due on the day of harvest, and do not be extravagant; surely He loves not the extravagant. And of the cattle — beasts of burden and those for slaughter. Eat of what God has provided you, and do not follow the steps of Satan; surely he is a manifest enemy to you.»}

And His saying: {«Say: Surely my prayer, my sacrifice, my life, and my death are for God, Lord of the worlds — no partner has He. With that I am commanded, and I am the first of the Muslims. Say: Shall I seek a lord other than God, when He is the Lord of everything? And every soul earns only against itself, and no bearer of burden bears the burden of another. Then to your Lord is your return, and He will inform you of what you differed about. And He it is who made you successors in the earth and raised some of you above others in degrees, that He might test you in what He has given you. Surely your Lord is swift in punishment, and surely He is Forgiving, Merciful.»}

And from Sūrat al-Aʿrāf, ten verses:
His saying, exalted be He: {«And We have established you in the earth and made for you therein means of livelihood — little do you give thanks. And We created you, then formed you, then said to the angels: Prostrate to Adam. So they prostrated, except Iblīs; he was not of those who prostrated.»}

And His saying: {«And they said: Praise be to God who guided us to this; we would not have been guided had God not guided us. Indeed, the messengers of our Lord came with the truth. And it was proclaimed to them: This is the Garden; you have been made to inherit it for what you used to do.»}

And His saying: {«Surely your Lord is God, who created the heavens and the earth in six days, then established Himself upon the Throne. He covers the night with the day, pursuing it swiftly; and the sun, the moon, and the stars are subjugated by His command. Surely His is the creation and the command. Blessed be God, Lord of the worlds. Call upon your Lord humbly and in secret; surely He loves not the transgressors. And do not corrupt the earth after its reformation, and call upon Him in fear and hope. Surely the mercy of God is near to the doers of good. And He it is who sends the winds as glad tidings before His mercy, until, when they carry heavy clouds, We drive them to a dead land and send down water upon it, and bring forth thereby fruits of every kind. Thus We bring forth the dead, that perhaps you may remember. And the good land — its vegetation comes forth by the permission of its Lord; and that which is bad — it comes forth only scantily. Thus We turn about the signs for a people who give thanks.»}

And His saying: {«And when Moses came to Our appointed time, and his Lord spoke to him, he said: My Lord, show me, that I may look upon You. He said: You shall not see Me; but look at the mountain — if it remains in its place, then you shall see Me. And when his Lord manifested Himself to the mountain, He made it crumble to dust, and Moses fell down stricken. When he recovered, he said: Glory be to You; I repent to You, and I am the first of the believers.»}

And His saying: {«Have they not looked upon the kingdom of the heavens and the earth, and what God has created of everything, and that perhaps their term has drawn near? In what discourse after this will they believe?»}

And from Sūrat al-Tawbah, four verses:
His saying, exalted be He: {«And they were commanded only to worship one God; there is no god but He. Glory be to Him above what they associate. They desire to extinguish the light of God with their mouths; but God refuses except to perfect His light, though the disbelievers dislike it. He it is who sent His Messenger with guidance and the religion of truth, to make it prevail over all religion, though the idolaters dislike it.»}

And His saying: {«Surely God — His is the kingdom of the heavens and the earth; He gives life and causes death; and you have, apart from God, no protector and no helper.»}

And from Sūrat Yūnus, eighteen verses:
His saying, exalted be He: {«Surely your Lord is God, who created the heavens and the earth in six days, then established Himself upon the Throne, directing the affair. There is no intercessor except after His permission. That is God, your Lord; so worship Him. Will you not remember? To Him is your return, all of you — the promise of God in truth. Surely He originates creation, then repeats it, that He may recompense those who believe and do righteous deeds with equity; and those who disbelieve — for them is a drink of boiling water and a painful chastisement, for what they used to disbelieve. He it is who made the sun a radiance and the moon a light, and decreed for it stations, that you might know the number of years and the reckoning. God created that only in truth, detailing the signs for a people who know. Surely in the alternation of the night and the day, and what God has created in the heavens and the earth, are signs for a people who are God-fearing.»}

And His saying: {«Say: Who provides for you from the sky and the earth? Who owns the hearing and the sight? Who brings forth the living from the dead and the dead from the living? Who directs the affair? They will say: God. Say: Will you not then fear? That is God, your Lord, the Truth. What is there after the truth except error? How then are you turned away?»}

And His saying: {«And you are not engaged in any affair, nor do you recite from Him any Qur'an, nor do you do any deed, but We are witnesses over you when you are immersed in it. And nothing escapes your Lord of the weight of an atom in the earth or in the sky, nor smaller than that nor greater, but it is in a clear Book.»}

And His saying: {«He it is who made for you the night that you might rest in it, and the day giving sight. Surely in that are signs for a people who hear. They say: God has taken a son. Glory be to Him; He is the Self-Sufficient. To Him belongs what is in the heavens and what is in the earth. You have no authority for this. Do you say about God what you do not know?»}

And His saying: {«And had your Lord willed, all who are on the earth would have believed, all of them together. Would you then compel people until they become believers? And it is not for a soul to believe except by the permission of God; and He lays abomination upon those who do not reason. Say: Look at what is in the heavens and the earth. But signs and warnings do not avail a people who do not believe.»}

And His saying: {«Say: O people, if you are in doubt about my religion — then I do not worship those you worship apart from God; but I worship God, who takes you in death, and I have been commanded to be of the believers. And that you set your face to the religion as a ḥanīf, and be not of the idolaters. And do not call, apart from God, upon what neither benefits you nor harms you; for if you do, then you are of the wrongdoers. And if God touches you with harm, there is no remover of it but He; and if He intends good for you, there is no repeller of His bounty. He causes it to reach whomever He wills of His servants; and He is the Forgiving, the Merciful. Say: O people, the truth has come to you from your Lord. So whoever is guided — it is only for his own soul; and whoever goes astray — it is only against it; and I am not a guardian over you. And follow what is revealed to you, and be patient until God judges; and He is the best of judges.»}

I say: And they are seven hundred and forty-one verses.

From Sūrat al-Baqarah, forty-six verses: His saying, the Exalted: {«In the name of God, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. Alif Lām Mīm. This is the Book about which there is no doubt, a guidance for the God-fearing—those who believe in the unseen, establish prayer, and spend from what We have provided them—and those who believe in what was revealed to you and what was revealed before you, and of the Hereafter they are certain. Those are upon guidance from their Lord, and it is they who are the successful.»} And His saying: {«O mankind, worship your Lord who created you and those before you, that you may become God-fearing.»} And His saying: {«O Children of Israel, remember My favor which I bestowed upon you, and fulfill My covenant, and I will fulfill your covenant, and fear Me alone. And believe in what I have revealed, confirming what is with you, and do not be the first to disbelieve in it, and do not exchange My verses for a small price, and fear Me alone. And do not clothe the truth with falsehood, nor conceal the truth while you know it. And establish prayer, and give zakāh, and bow with those who bow. Do you command people to righteousness and forget yourselves while you recite the Book? Will you not then reason? And seek help through patience and prayer; and indeed, it is difficult except for the humble—those who are certain that they will meet their Lord and that to Him they will return.»} And His saying: {«Then your hearts became hardened after that, so they were like stones or even harder. And indeed, from stones there are those from which rivers burst forth, and indeed, from them there are those that split open and water comes out, and indeed, from them there are those that fall down for fear of God. And God is not unaware of what you do. Do you then hope that they will believe for you, while a party of them used to hear the word of God and then distort it after they had understood it, while they knew?»} And His saying: {«And establish prayer and give zakāh; then you turned away, except a few of you, and you were refusing.»} And His saying: {«Yes, whoever submits his face to God while he is a doer of good—he will have his reward with his Lord, and no fear will be upon them, nor will they grieve.»} And His saying: {«So remember Me; I will remember you. And be grateful to Me and do not deny Me. O you who have believed, seek help through patience and prayer. Indeed, God is with the patient. And do not say about those who are killed in the cause of God that they are dead; rather, they are alive, but you do not perceive. And We will surely test you with something of fear and hunger and a loss of wealth and lives and fruits, but give good tidings to the patient—those who, when disaster strikes them, say, "Indeed, we belong to God, and indeed, to Him we will return." Those are the ones upon whom are blessings from their Lord and mercy, and it is they who are the guided.»} And His saying: {«O mankind, eat from whatever is on earth that is lawful and good, and do not follow the footsteps of Satan. Indeed, he is to you a clear enemy. He only commands you to evil and immorality and to say about God what you do not know.»} And His saying: {«Righteousness is not that you turn your faces toward the east or the west, but righteousness is [in] one who believes in God, the Last Day, the angels, the Book, and the prophets, and gives wealth, despite love for it, to relatives, orphans, the needy, the traveler, those who ask, and for freeing slaves; and establishes prayer and gives zakāh; and those who fulfill their covenant when they make a promise, and the patient in poverty and hardship and during battle. Those are the ones who have been true, and it is they who are the God-fearing.»} And His saying: {«And fear God and know that God is with the God-fearing. And spend in the cause of God and do not throw yourselves into destruction, and do good; indeed, God loves the doers of good.»} And His saying: {«Indeed, those who have believed and those who have emigrated and fought in the cause of God—those expect the mercy of God. And God is Forgiving and Merciful.»} And His saying: {«And know that God knows what is within yourselves, so beware of Him. And know that God is Forgiving and Forbearing.»} And His saying: {«The example of those who spend their wealth in the cause of God is like a seed that grows seven ears; in every ear is a hundred grains. And God multiplies for whom He wills, and God is All-Encompassing and Knowing. Those who spend their wealth in the cause of God and then do not follow up what they spent with reminders or injury—they will have their reward with their Lord, and no fear will be upon them, nor will they grieve.»} And His saying: {«O you who have believed, fear God and give up what remains of interest, if you should be believers. And if you do not, then be informed of a war from God and His Messenger. But if you repent, you may have your principal—neither wronging nor being wronged. And if someone is in hardship, then deferment until ease. And to give charity is better for you, if you only knew. And fear a Day when you will be returned to God; then every soul will be paid in full for what it has earned, and they will not be wronged.»} And His saying: {«To God belongs whatever is in the heavens and whatever is in the earth. Whether you show what is within yourselves or conceal it, God will bring you to account for it. Then He will forgive whom He wills and punish whom He wills, and God is over all things competent. The Messenger has believed in what was revealed to him from his Lord, and the believers, all of them have believed in God and His angels and His books and His messengers, saying, "We make no distinction between any of His messengers." And they say, "We hear and we obey. We seek Your forgiveness, our Lord, and to You is the final destination." God does not charge a soul except with what is within its capacity. It will have what it has earned, and upon it will be what it has incurred. "Our Lord, do not impose blame upon us if we have forgotten or erred. Our Lord, and lay not upon us a burden like that which You laid upon those before us. Our Lord, and burden us not with that which we have no ability to bear. And pardon us, and forgive us, and have mercy upon us. You are our protector, so give us victory over the disbelieving people."»}

And from Sūrat Āl ʿImrān, thirty-four verses: His saying, the Exalted: {«It is He who has sent down upon you the Book, in which are verses precise—they are the mother of the Book—and others unspecific. As for those in whose hearts is deviation, they follow what is unspecific of it, seeking discord and seeking its interpretation. And no one knows its interpretation except God. And those firm in knowledge say, "We believe in it; all of it is from our Lord." And no one will be reminded except those of understanding. "Our Lord, let not our hearts deviate after You have guided us and grant us from Yourself mercy. Indeed, You are the Bestower. Our Lord, surely You will gather the people for a Day about which there is no doubt. Indeed, God does not fail in His promise."»} And His saying: {«Beautified for people is the love of that which they desire—of women and sons and heaped-up sums of gold and silver and fine branded horses and cattle and tilled land. That is the enjoyment of worldly life, but God has with Him the best return. Say, "Shall I inform you of better than that? For those who fear God will be gardens in the presence of their Lord beneath which rivers flow, wherein they abide eternally, and purified spouses and approval from God. And God is Seeing of the servants—those who say, 'Our Lord, indeed we have believed, so forgive us our sins and protect us from the punishment of the Fire'—the patient, the truthful, the devoutly obedient, the spenders, and the seekers of forgiveness before dawn.»} And His saying: {«Let not believers take disbelievers as allies instead of believers. And whoever does that has nothing with God, except when taking precaution against them in prudence. And God warns you of Himself, and to God is the final destination.»} And His saying: {«Say, "If you should love God, then follow me, and God will love you and forgive you your sins. And God is Forgiving and Merciful." Say, "Obey God and the Messenger." But if they turn away—then indeed, God does not love the disbelievers.»} And His saying: {«So is it other than the religion of God they desire, while to Him have submitted all those within the heavens and earth, willingly or by compulsion, and to Him they will be returned?»} And His saying: {«Never will you attain righteousness until you spend from that which you love. And whatever you spend—indeed, God is Knowing of it.»} And His saying: {«O you who have believed, fear God as He should be feared and do not die except as Muslims. And hold firmly to the rope of God all together and do not become divided. And remember the favor of God upon you when you were enemies and He brought your hearts together and you became, by His favor, brothers. And you were on the edge of a pit of the Fire, and He saved you from it. Thus does God make clear to you His verses that you may be guided. And let there be from you a nation inviting to good, enjoining what is right and forbidding what is wrong, and it is they who are the successful.»} And His saying: {«They are not all alike. Among the People of the Book is a community standing, reciting the verses of God during the hours of the night while prostrating. They believe in God and the Last Day, and they enjoin what is right and forbid what is wrong and hasten to good deeds. And those are among the righteous. And whatever good they do—never will it be denied them. And God is Knowing of the God-fearing. Indeed, those who disbelieve—never will their wealth or their children avail them against God at all, and those are the companions of the Fire; they will abide therein eternally. The example of what they spend in this worldly life is like that of a wind containing frost which strikes the harvest of a people who have wronged themselves and destroys it. And God did not wrong them, but they wronged themselves.»} And His saying: {«Not for you is the decision whether He will forgive them or punish them, for indeed, they are wrongdoers. And to God belongs whatever is in the heavens and whatever is in the earth. He forgives whom He wills and punishes whom He wills. And God is Forgiving and Merciful.»} And His saying: {«And hasten to forgiveness from your Lord and a garden as wide as the heavens and the earth, prepared for the God-fearing—those who spend in ease and hardship and who restrain anger and who pardon the people. And God loves the doers of good. And those who, when they commit an immorality or wrong themselves, remember God and seek forgiveness for their sins—and who can forgive sins except God?—and do not persist in what they did while they know. Those—their reward is forgiveness from their Lord and gardens beneath which rivers flow, wherein they abide eternally. And excellent is the reward of the workers.»} And His saying: {«And it is not for a soul to die except by God's permission, a decree determined. And whoever desires the reward of this world—We will give him from it; and whoever desires the reward of the Hereafter—We will give him from it. And We will reward the grateful.»} And His saying: {«So by mercy from God, you were lenient with them. And if you had been rude and harsh in heart, they would have disbanded from about you. So pardon them and ask forgiveness for them and consult them in the matter. And when you have decided, then rely upon God. Indeed, God loves those who rely upon Him.»} And His saying: {«And let not those who are stingy with what God has given them of His bounty think that it is better for them. Rather, it is worse for them. They will be encircled by what they withheld on the Day of Resurrection. And to God belongs the inheritance of the heavens and the earth, and God is Acquainted with what you do.»} And His saying: {«Do not think those who rejoice in what they have brought and love to be praised for what they have not done—do not think them safe from punishment, and for them is a painful punishment.»} And His saying: {«O you who have believed, be patient and endure in patience and remain stationed and fear God, that you may be successful.»}

And from Sūrat al-Nisāʾ, fifty-nine verses: His saying, the Exalted: {«O mankind, fear your Lord, who created you from one soul and created from it its mate and dispersed from both of them many men and women. And fear God, through whom you ask one another, and the wombs. Indeed, God is ever, over you, an Observer.»} And His saying: {«God wants to make clear to you and guide you to the ways of those before you and to accept your repentance. And God is Knowing and Wise. And God wants to accept your repentance, but those who follow desires want you to deviate greatly. And God wants to lighten for you, and mankind was created weak.»} And His saying: {«If you avoid the great sins which you are forbidden, We will remove from you your lesser sins and admit you to a noble entrance. And do not wish for that by which God has made some of you exceed others. For men is a share of what they have earned, and for women is a share of what they have earned. And ask God of His bounty. Indeed, God is ever, over all things, Knowing.»} And His saying: {«Worship God and associate nothing with Him, and to parents do good, and to relatives, orphans, the needy, the near neighbor, the distant neighbor, the companion at your side, the traveler, and those whom your right hands possess. Indeed, God does not like those who are self-deluding and boastful—who are stingy and enjoin people to stinginess and conceal what God has given them of His bounty. And We have prepared for the disbelievers a humiliating punishment. And those who spend their wealth to be seen by people and believe not in God nor in the Last Day. And whoever has Satan as a companion—then evil is he as a companion. And what would it harm them if they believed in God and the Last Day and spent from what God has provided for them? And God is ever, about them, Knowing. Indeed, God does not wrong even the weight of an atom. And if there is a good deed, He multiplies it and gives from Himself a great reward. So how will it be when We bring from every nation a witness and We bring you, O Muhammad, against these as a witness?»} And His saying: {«Indeed, God does not forgive association with Him, but He forgives what is less than that for whom He wills. And he who associates others with God has certainly fabricated a tremendous sin. Have you not seen those who claim purity for themselves? Rather, God purifies whom He wills, and they will not be wronged even the size of a thread.»} And His saying: {«Indeed, God commands you to render trusts to their owners and, when you judge between people, to judge with justice. Excellent is that which God instructs you. Indeed, God is ever Hearing and Seeing. O you who have believed, obey God and obey the Messenger and those in authority among you. And if you disagree over anything, refer it to God and the Messenger, if you should believe in God and the Last Day. That is better and more suitable in final result.»} And His saying: {«And We sent not a messenger except to be obeyed by permission of God. And if, when they wronged themselves, they had come to you and asked forgiveness of God and the Messenger had asked forgiveness for them, they would have found God Accepting of repentance and Merciful. But no, by your Lord, they will not believe until they make you judge concerning that over which they dispute among themselves and then find within themselves no discomfort from what you have judged and submit in full, willing submission.»} And His saying: {«And whoever obeys God and the Messenger—those will be with the ones upon whom God has bestowed favor of the prophets, the steadfast affirmers of truth, the martyrs, and the righteous. And excellent are those as companions. That is the bounty from God, and sufficient is God as Knower.»} And His saying: {«What comes to you of good is from God, but what comes to you of evil is from yourself. And We sent you to the people as a messenger, and sufficient is God as Witness. Whoever obeys the Messenger has obeyed God; but whoever turns away—We have not sent you over them as a guardian.»} And His saying: {«And rely upon God; and sufficient is God as Disposer of affairs. Then do they not reflect upon the Qur'an? If it had been from other than God, they would have found within it much contradiction. And when there comes to them an matter of security or fear, they publicize it. But if they had referred it to the Messenger or to those in authority among them, those among them who can investigate it would have known it. And if not for the favor of God upon you and His mercy, you would have followed Satan, except for a few.»} And His saying: {«Whoever intercedes for a good cause will have a share from it, and whoever intercedes for an evil cause will have a burden from it. And God is ever, over all things, a Keeper. And when you are greeted with a greeting, greet with better than it or return it. Indeed, God is ever, over all things, an Accountant. God—there is no deity except Him. He will surely assemble you on the Day of Resurrection, about which there is no doubt. And who is more truthful than God in statement?»} And His saying: {«O you who have believed, when you go forth in the cause of God, investigate, and do not say to one who gives you the greeting of peace, "You are not a believer," aspiring to the goods of worldly life; for with God are many acquisitions. You were like that before; then God conferred His favor upon you, so investigate. Indeed, God is ever, with what you do, Acquainted. Not equal are those believers remaining at home—other than the disabled—and the mujāhidūn in the cause of God with their wealth and their lives. God has preferred the mujāhidūn with their wealth and their lives over those remaining at home by a degree. And to all God has promised the best. And God has preferred the mujāhidūn over those remaining at home with a great reward—degrees from Him and forgiveness and mercy. And God is ever Forgiving and Merciful.»} And His saying: {«And when you have completed the prayer, remember God standing, sitting, or on your sides. And when you become secure, establish prayer. Indeed, prayer has been upon the believers a decree at specified times. And do not weaken in pursuit of the enemy. If you are suffering, indeed, they are suffering as you are suffering, but you expect from God that which they do not expect. And God is ever Knowing and Wise. Indeed, We have revealed to you the Book in truth so you may judge between the people by that which God has shown you. And do not be an advocate for the treacherous. And seek forgiveness of God. Indeed, God is ever Forgiving and Merciful. And do not argue on behalf of those who betray themselves. Indeed, God does not like one who is habitually sinful and treacherous.»} And His saying: {«And whoever does a wrong or wrongs himself but then seeks forgiveness of God will find God Forgiving and Merciful. And whoever earns a sin only earns it against himself. And God is ever Knowing and Wise. And whoever earns a mistake or a sin and then blames it on an innocent person has taken upon himself a slander and manifest sin. And if not for the favor of God upon you and His mercy, a group of them would have determined to mislead you. But they do not mislead except themselves, and they will not harm you at all. And God has revealed to you the Book and wisdom and has taught you that which you did not know. And ever has the favor of God upon you been great. No good is there in much of their private conversation, except for those who enjoin charity or that which is right or conciliation between people. And whoever does that seeking approval of God—then We are going to give him a great reward. And whoever opposes the Messenger after guidance has become clear to him and follows other than the way of the believers—We will give him what he has taken and drive him into Hell, and evil it is as a destination. Indeed, God does not forgive association with Him, but He forgives what is less than that for whom He wills. And he who associates others with God has certainly gone far astray.»} And His saying: {«And who is better in religion than one who submits his face to God while being a doer of good and follows the religion of Abraham, inclining toward truth? And God took Abraham as an intimate friend. And to God belongs whatever is in the heavens and whatever is in the earth. And ever has God encompassed all things.»} And His saying: {«And you will never be able to be equal between wives, even if you should strive. So do not incline completely and leave another hanging. And if you amend and fear God—then indeed, God is ever Forgiving and Merciful.»} And His saying: {«Except for those who repent, reform, hold fast to God, and are sincere in their religion for God—those will be with the believers. And God is going to give the believers a great reward. What would God do with your punishment if you are grateful and believe? And ever is God Appreciative and Knowing. God does not like the public mention of evil except by one who has been wronged. And ever is God Hearing and Knowing. If you disclose a good deed or conceal it or pardon an evil—then indeed, God is ever Pardoning and Competent.»} And His saying: {«But those firm in knowledge among them and the believers believe in what has been revealed to you and what was revealed before you. And the establishers of prayer and the givers of zakāh and the believers in God and the Last Day—those We will give a great reward.»} And His saying: {«O mankind, there has come to you a conclusive proof from your Lord, and We have sent down to you a clear light. So as for those who believe in God and hold fast to Him—He will admit them to mercy from Himself and bounty and guide them to Himself on a straight path.»}

And from Sūrat al-Māʾidah, twelve verses: His saying, the Exalted: {«And cooperate in righteousness and piety, but do not cooperate in sin and aggression. And fear God; indeed, God is severe in penalty. Prohibited to you are dead animals, blood, the flesh of swine, and that which has been dedicated to other than God, and those killed by strangling or by a violent blow or by a headlong fall or by the goring of horns, and those from which a wild animal has eaten, except what you slaughter, and those sacrificed on stone altars, and [prohibited is] that you seek decision through divining arrows. That is grave disobedience. This day those who disbelieve have despaired of your religion, so fear them not, but fear Me. This day I have perfected for you your religion and completed My favor upon you and have approved for you Islam as religion. But whoever is forced by severe hunger with no inclination to sin—then indeed, God is Forgiving and Merciful.»} And His saying: {«O you who have believed, be persistently standing firm for God, witnesses in justice, and do not let the hatred of a people prevent you from being just. Be just; that is nearer to righteousness. And fear God; indeed, God is Acquainted with what you do. God has promised those who believe and do righteous deeds forgiveness and a great reward.»} And His saying: {«O you who have believed, fear God and seek the means to Him and strive in His cause, that you may succeed.»} And His saying: {«And judge between them by what God has revealed and do not follow their inclinations and beware of them, lest they tempt you away from some of what God has revealed to you. And if they turn away—then know that God only intends to afflict them with some of their sins. And indeed, many among the people are defiantly disobedient. Then is it the judgement of ignorance they desire? But who is better than God in judgement for a people who are certain?»} And His saying: {«And when they hear what has been revealed to the Messenger, you see their eyes overflowing with tears because of what they have recognized of the truth. They say, "Our Lord, we have believed, so register us among the witnesses. And why should we not believe in God and what has come to us of the truth? And we aspire that our Lord will admit us with the righteous people." So God rewarded them for what they said with gardens beneath which rivers flow, wherein they abide eternally. And that is the reward of doers of good.»} And His saying: {«There is not upon those who believe and do righteous deeds any blame concerning what they have eaten if they fear God and believe and do righteous deeds, and then fear God and believe, and then fear God and do good. And God loves the doers of good.»} And His saying: {«O you who have believed, upon you is responsibility for yourselves. Those who have gone astray will not harm you when you have been guided. To God is your return all together, and He will inform you of what you used to do.»}

And from Sūrat al-Anʿām, seventeen verses: His saying, the Exalted: {«And the worldly life is not but amusement and diversion, and the home of the Hereafter is better for those who fear God. Will you not then reason?»} And His saying: {«So when they forgot that by which they had been reminded, We opened to them the doors of every thing until, when they rejoiced in what they were given, We seized them suddenly, and they were in despair. So the roots of the people who wronged were cut off. And all praise is due to God, Lord of the worlds.»} And His saying: {«And do not drive away those who call upon their Lord morning and evening, seeking His countenance. Not upon you is anything of their account, and not upon them is anything of your account. So drive them not away and thus be of the wrongdoers. And thus We have tried some of them through others that they might say, "Are these the ones whom God has favored among us?" Is not God most knowing of the grateful? And when those who believe in Our verses come to you, say, "Peace be upon you. Your Lord has decreed upon Himself mercy: that whoever among you does wrong out of ignorance and then repents after that and reforms—then indeed, He is Forgiving and Merciful."»} And His saying: {«And when you see those who engage in discourse concerning Our verses, then turn away from them until they enter into another conversation. And if Satan should cause you to forget, then do not remain after the reminder with the wrongdoing people. And those who fear God are not accountable for them at all, but [only for] a reminder; perhaps they will fear Him.»} And His saying: {«Those who believe and do not mix their belief with injustice—those will have security, and they are guided.»} And His saying: {«And leave apparent sin and hidden sin. Indeed, those who earn sin will be recompensed for what they used to commit.»} And His saying: {«So whoever God wants to guide—He expands his breast to Islam. And whoever He wants to mislead—He makes his breast tight and constricted, as though he were climbing into the sky. Thus does God place defilement upon those who do not believe. And this is the path of your Lord, leading straight. We have detailed the verses for a people who remember. For them will be the Home of Peace with their Lord. And He will be their protector because of what they used to do.»} And His saying: {«And do not approach immoralities—what is apparent of them and what is internal. And do not kill the soul which God has forbidden, except by right. That is what He has instructed you, that you may reason. And do not approach the property of an orphan except in the way that is best, until he reaches maturity. And give full measure and weight in justice. We do not charge any soul except with what is within its capacity. And when you speak, be just, even if it concerns a relative. And fulfill the covenant of God. That is what He has instructed you, that you may remember. And indeed, this is My straight path, so follow it, and do not follow other paths, for they will separate you from His path. That is what He has instructed you, that you may become God-fearing.»} And His saying: {«Whoever comes with a good deed will have ten times the like thereof, and whoever comes with an evil deed will not be recompensed except with the like thereof, and they will not be wronged.»}

And from Sūrat al-Aʿrāf, eight verses: His saying, the Exalted: {«Say, "My Lord has commanded justice, and set your faces at every place of prayer and call upon Him, being sincere to Him in religion. Just as He originated you, you will return." A group He has guided, and a group has deserved error because they have taken the devils as allies instead of God and think that they are guided. O children of Adam, take your adornment at every place of prayer, and eat and drink, but be not excessive. Indeed, He does not like those who commit excess.»} And His saying: {«And if only the people of the cities had believed and feared God, We would have opened upon them blessings from the heaven and the earth; but they denied, so We seized them for what they used to earn.»} And His saying: {«So when they forgot that by which they had been reminded, We saved those who had forbidden evil and seized those who wronged with a wretched punishment, because they were defiantly disobeying.»} And His saying: {«And when you do not bring them a sign, they say, "Why have you not contrived it?" Say, "I only follow what is revealed to me from my Lord. This is insight from your Lord and guidance and mercy for a people who believe." And when the Qur'an is recited, then listen to it and pay attention that you may receive mercy. And remember your Lord within yourself in humility and in fear and without being apparent in speech—in the mornings and the evenings. And do not be among the heedless. Indeed, those who are with your Lord are not prevented by arrogance from His worship, and they exalt Him, and to Him they prostrate.»}

And from Sūrat al-Anfāl, eleven verses: His saying: {«They ask you about the spoils of war. Say, "The spoils of war are for God and the Messenger." So fear God and amend that which is between you and obey God and His Messenger, if you should be believers. The believers are only those who, when God is mentioned, their hearts become fearful, and when His verses are recited to them, it increases them in faith; and upon their Lord they rely—those who establish prayer and from what We have provided them spend. Those are the believers, truly. For them are degrees with their Lord and forgiveness and noble provision.»} And His saying: {«O you who have believed, respond to God and to the Messenger when He calls you to that which gives you life. And know that God intervenes between a man and his heart and that to Him you will be gathered. And fear a trial which will not strike those who have wronged among you exclusively, and know that God is severe in penalty. And remember when you were few and oppressed in the land, fearing that people might abduct you, and He sheltered you and supported you with His victory and provided you from good things—that you might be grateful. O you who have believed, do not betray God and the Messenger or betray your trusts while you know. And know that your properties and your children are but a trial and that God has with Him a great reward.»} And His saying: {«That is because God would not change a favor which He had bestowed upon a people until they change what is within themselves. And indeed, God is Hearing and Knowing.»}

And from Sūrat al-Tawbah, twelve verses: His saying, the Exalted: {«The mosques of God are only maintained by those who believe in God and the Last Day and establish prayer and give zakāh and do not fear except God. It is expected that those will be of the guided.»} And His saying: {«Say, "If your fathers, your sons, your brothers, your wives, your relatives, wealth which you have obtained, commerce wherein you fear decline, and dwellings with which you are pleased are more beloved to you than God and His Messenger and jihad in His cause, then wait until God executes His command. And God does not guide the defiantly disobedient people."»} And His saying: {«O you who have believed, what is with you that when it is said to you, "Go forth in the cause of God," you sink heavily to the ground? Are you satisfied with the life of this world rather than the Hereafter? But what is the enjoyment of worldly life compared to the Hereafter except a little.»} And His saying: {«And the believing men and believing women are allies of one another. They enjoin what is right and forbid what is wrong and establish prayer and give zakāh and obey God and His Messenger. Those—God will have mercy upon them. Indeed, God is Exalted in Might and Wise.»} And His saying: {«And the first forerunners among the Muhājirūn and the Anṣār and those who followed them with good conduct—God is pleased with them and they are pleased with Him, and He has prepared for them gardens beneath which rivers flow, wherein they abide forever. That is the great attainment.»} And His saying: {«Do they not know that
